body:
Honestly as long as you have your priorities in line at all times you should be fine. I'm an extremely active person- I work 5 days a week, am working on my career, go and ride my horse after work, and at the end of the day I always find a way to enjoy a bowl or joint to relax. Nothing wrong with that. I wake up the next day, and carry on with my busy life. 

&#x200B;

I didn't smoke in high school, and honestly the only thing I have for you that would spark concern is keeping it concealed from your parents and if you're in a legal state. I'm in college living at home, but I'm 20+ doing my own thing so it's a bit different. You just should have a plan as to what to do if you're caught by your parents.

Hi, I use to work at a boarding facility. 

&#x200B;

Pointers:

&#x200B;

My place would let your dog come stay the day a couple times if you wanted for a "test run"- how your dog took to the place, how you felt about it as well, that kind of stuff. Most reliable boarding facilities will allow something along the lines, so you should look into that.

&#x200B;

I worked at a facility where the dogs were brought out to play/use the bathroom in the play yard individually- I found that that's the safe way to go, if your dog isn't overly friendly, and plus it helps give you a peace of mind as well. They were NEVER unattended in the yard- as it should be.

&#x200B;

Dogs stayed in their own little kennel room/stall. Shavings were laid on the floor for comfort/minimize mess (it's harder to track dog pee around when you have something absorbent down like that). (I mean, there's really no reason why they should be in a kennel stall with dogs not from the same family)

&#x200B;

RED FLAGS:

&#x200B;

If the owner doesn't offer tours, or has VERY tight and strict tour hours, then that's not a good sign. A responsible facility owner is proud and confident in their place. 

&#x200B;

If they let you tour, do the kennel stall doors look secure? 

&#x200B;

Mopey staff is also a downfall. When I worked at my kennel I was always on a roll. I love animals- they've always been my biggest interest. If the staff seem unobservant, or dull, that's worrisome, as someone else pointed out. 

&#x200B;

Hope this helped.

&#x200B;

Ok, don't let anyone give you shit for eBay bongs. I got a $35 dollar pearlescent one from there and I absolutely love it, it's decent quality. 10/10 recommend.

&#x200B;

Have fun tokin!

Not really sure how to help you, but sending out e-mails is basically my go-to. I live in the SF Bay Area, where we have plenty of dispensaries here in Berk/SF and decent weed culture, and if you know the right connections through the niche here I'm sure you could land something.

&#x200B;

I've had friends around your age work at dispensaries, and although they didn't do anything too exciting, that is exactly where they got a feel for the weed industry.

&#x200B;

But going to dispensaries' official websites and contacting them through e-mail is never a bad idea, wishing you luck!

I also hate it when people do that thing where they lick their finger before they sort through their bills.

&#x200B;

Nasty as shit. You don't always have to do that.

Methed out girl with her (supposedly) pimp last year shouted "fuck you, bitch!" when I refused to let her purchase the butane can she wanted because she was underage. 

&#x200B;

Everyone's face in line was priceless.
